<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sheffield Shield standings after</p>
<p>the final round of matches were completed on Sunday (tabulate</p>
<p>under played, won outright, won on first innings, drawn, lost on</p>
<p>first innings, lost outright, points):</p>
<p> Western Australia   10   6   3   0   0   1   42</p>
<p> Queensland	    10   4   2   0   3   1   28</p>
<p> New South Wales     10   4   1   0   1   4   28</p>
<p> Tasmania		10   3   2   0   1   4   28</p>
<p> Victoria		10   3   0   0   2   5   19.7</p>
<p> South Australia     10   2   0   0   1   7   14</p>
<p>Note: Victoria deducted 0.3 of a point for slow over rate</p>
<p>against New South Wales.</p>
<p>Queensland qualify for Shield final against Western</p>
<p>Australia from March 21-25 in Perth with a superior average of</p>
<p>runs scored for and against during the season.</p>
</text>
